8. History of malignancy, radiotherapy, or chemotherapy for any malignancy within the last 5 years. History of malignancy may include: Multiple exostoses syndrome ((also known as multiple osteochondromas syndrome), an inherited condition associated with bumps of cartilage on the bones, has been associated with an increased risk of chondrosarcoma), any cancer prone syndrome, such as Li-Fraumeni;
9. Any autoimmune disease (e.g. Systemic Lupus Erythematosus or dermatomyositis);
